SUMMARY:Walk: Gatineau Corridor Trail! 9KM
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌿 Gatineau Corridor Trail Wal
 k\n\n### An Easy\, Flat Walk — Perfect for Getting Started\n\nWe'll begi
 n near Kennedy Station and make our way through a series of small parks be
 fore connecting with the Gatineau Corridor Trail. Along the way\, we'll pa
 ss through areas filled with wildflowers\, tall grasses\, and natural grow
 th that give you a glimpse of what these spaces can look like when nature 
 is allowed to take over a little. 🌼🌿\n\nThe city has changed the way
  some of these green spaces are maintained\, allowing the grass and wildfl
 owers to grow more naturally. Instead of perfectly manicured lawns\, you'l
 l see a much more colourful and natural landscape — a little reminder th
 at sometimes the most beautiful parts of the city are the ones we simply l
 et grow.\n\nDon't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE!](ht
 tps://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂
 ️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll start at the Dollar Tree and walk through the s
 urrounding green spaces before joining the Gatineau Corridor Trail.\n\nAlo
 ng the way we'll:\n\n* Walk through several small parks\n* Follow the most
 ly flat trail\n* Lots of wildflowers\n* Stop for a break around Eglinton &
  Victoria Park\n* Enjoy some conversation and time to get to know each oth
 er\n* Make our way back to where we started\n\nThe walk is approximately *
 *2hrs** depending on the pace of the group.\nAnd remember — **you can le
 ave at any time.**\nThere are multiple points along the route where you ca
 n make your own way home.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nTh
 is walk happens in typical Toronto weather conditions.\nPlease dress appro
 priately for the weather and bring water\, especially during the warmer mo
 nths.\nThis is one of our easier walks. If you've been wanting to start wa
 lking more but aren't sure you're ready for a longer or more challenging h
 ike\, **this is a great place to begin.**\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details
 \n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of the Dollar Tree Store\n🫎 I'll
  be wearing my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM**\nI will only wait
  5 minutes.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚗 **Parking:** The
 re is parking available in the area.\n🚇 **Transit:** We're also relativ
 ely close to Kennedy Station.\n\n🏁 **End Point:** Back at the Dollar Tr
 ee Store\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-trans
 fer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com
 )**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing
  events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\
 n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧴 Sunscreen on sunny day
 s\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is especially great for:
 \n\n* People who are getting back into walking\n* Anyone looking for an ea
 sy trail\n* Beginners who aren't ready for a challenging hike\n* People wh
 o want to meet others while getting some fresh air\n* Anyone who simply wa
 nts an easy Saturday/Sunday outing\n\nThe activity is the container. **The
  people you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\n***\n\nREMEMB
 ER: You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you
 're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may ne
 ed to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page fo
 r updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wal
 l or email:\n**[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesa
 ndoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for the easy trail.**\n**Stay for the c
 onversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.*
 * 🌿💛
