SUMMARY:The Sunday Night with Friends Dinner Party (September 13th) 
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nGood day everyone\,\n\nJoin us for
  **The Sunday Night with Friends Dinner Party**\, a warm and welcoming eve
 ning created for meeting new people\, enjoying good conversation and shari
 ng a relaxed meal together. Whether you arrive with friends or come on you
 r own\, you’ll be welcomed into a friendly social atmosphere.\n\n\\*Join
 ed by my other social groups too\; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn ou
 t with lots of friendly peers to begin our weekend with!\n\n\\*Please note
  we are at **The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 b
 locks north of Lawrence - south of the 401 **(we will be in the back dinin
 g area)**\n\n*\\*You can ask the bartender if you like to show you to the 
 group (simply ask for Steve's dinner party)*\n\n-You'll find it's a cozy\,
  relaxed and enjoyable atmosphere!\n\n**-Free Parking found on residential
  side streets**\n\n(Event Details Below)\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\
 n(Organizer/Host)\n\nEvent Details:\n**The Sunday Night with Friends Dinne
 r Party**\n\nLooking for a fun and relaxed way to enjoy your Sunday evenin
 g?\n\n\\*\\*Highlights:\\*\\*\n\n\\* 🍽️ Enjoy a delicious dinner in a
  relaxed\, friendly setting.\n\\* 😊 Meet new people and reconnect with 
 familiar faces.\n\\* 💬 Great conversation\, laughter\, and a welcoming 
 social atmosphere.\n\n**Dinner Party Topics** may include but not limited 
 too: Travel\, Culture\, Spirituality\, Relationships\, Modern Dating\, Wor
 k/Life balance\, Life after Marriage\, Dating Apps\, Comedy\, History\, Ar
 t\, Technology\, Economy\, Music\, Movies\, Sports\, Fashion\, Hobbies\, B
 ooks\, Psychology\, Philosophy\, the Future\, History\, Pop Culture\, Thea
 tre\, etc.)\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:** 5 dollars (Cash only at the
  door) (HST included)\nor by e transfer: **steveflemming11@gmail.com**\n\n
 ***\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\n-Arrive any time between 6:30 pm and 7:3
 0 pm (if you can) (please ask for Steve when you arrive- we will either be
  inside or on the patio-depending on weather and our numbers)\n\n\\*Great 
 dinner menu and food specials provided:\n(One beverage or appetizer minimu
 m upon arrival to support venue)\n\n**Parking and Transportation:**\n\\*Lo
 ts of street parking on avenue and free residential parking\nhttps://www.f
 irkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/\n\n(15-20 minute walk from Yonge & Law
 rence subway station-or simply take bus or uber from the station)
