SUMMARY:The Saturday with Friends High Park Walk and Roncesvalles Polish F
 estival!
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nHello everyone\,\n\n**\\*\\*Please
  kindly read carefully- Thank you\\*\\***\n\nJoin us for a wonderful Satur
 day afternoon of walking\, conversation\, culture and new friendships! We
 ’ll enjoy the natural beauty of **High Park** before continuing to the l
 ively **Roncesvalles Polish Festival\,** where the neighbourhood comes ali
 ve with music\, entertainment\, food and community spirit.\nWhether you’
 re coming alone or bringing a friend\, you’ll be warmly welcomed. This i
 s a relaxed social outing designed for people who enjoy exploring Toronto\
 , meeting others and sharing good conversation along the way.\n\nWe will m
 eet at **La Diperie Cafe** where you are welcome to grab a coffee\, water\
 , pastry or ice cream if you like before we head out.\n\nThis will give us
  an opportunity to introduce ourselves as everyone arrives\; then make our
  way on a friendly walk through the iconic **High Park in Toronto.**\n\nEv
 ent Details below:\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Host/Organizer)\n\n*
 *Event Details:**\n**The Saturday with Friends High Park Walk and Roncesva
 lles Polish Festival!**\n\nOur afternoon will begin with a leisurely walk 
 through High Park\, one of Toronto’s most beautiful green spaces. We’l
 l stroll at a comfortable pace\, take in the scenery and have plenty of op
 portunities to talk and get to know one another.\n\nAfter our walk\, we’
 ll make our way toward Roncesvalles Avenue to experience the Polish Festiv
 al. You can enjoy the festive atmosphere\, live entertainment\, cultural d
 isplays and a tempting variety of Polish food and treats.\n\n###\n\n**High
 lights:**\n\n* Take a relaxing and scenic walk through High Park\n* Meet f
 riendly people and make new connections\n* Explore the Roncesvalles neighb
 ourhood\n* Experience Polish music\, culture\, food and entertainment\n* E
 njoy a fun and welcoming Saturday afternoon in Toronto\n\nPlease wear comf
 ortable walking shoes and dress for the weather. Everyone is responsible f
 or purchasing their own food\, drinks and other items during the festival.
 \nCome with a friendly attitude\, an open mind and a willingness to connec
 t. Let’s walk\, laugh\, explore and enjoy a memorable Saturday together!
 \n\n**Event Fee:** 10 dollars when you arrive at the La Diperie Cafe (cash
  only please)\nor e transfer in advance to **steveflemming11@gmail.com**\n
 \n\\*I strongly encourage you to take the subway as it is very close to th
 e cafe but certainly driving in an option\n\\*Street parking will be found
  along Bloor Street and residential area but not inside the park\n\n**Time
  and Location: Where to meet us?**\n(Please arrive on time :)\n\nMeet us a
 t **La Diperie Cafe** at 2:30 p.m.\n(we will wait for everyone until 3:00 
 p.m.)\n**Address:** 1960 Bloor St W\, Toronto\, ON M4W 1J2\nVery close to 
 the High Park Subway station\n(We will then head out for our walk at that 
 point)
