SUMMARY:🌿🚶‍♂️ YORK BELTLINE TRAIL & Brunch! 🍻🌿
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌿🚶‍♂️ YORK BELTLINE 
 TRAIL & BRUNCH 🍻🌿\n\n**A Hidden Urban Trail\, Easy Walking & A Relax
 ing Summer Sunday**\nLooking for an easy way to get outside after work?\n\
 nJoin us for a summer walk along the York Beltline Trail\, one of Toronto'
 s hidden green corridors.\n\nBuilt on the route of the historic Belt Line 
 Railway\, this peaceful trail offers a surprising escape from the city\, w
 ith mature trees\, birdsong\, and plenty of shade—all just steps from th
 e subway.\nThis is an easy\, mostly flat walk with no major hills\, making
  it perfect for anyone who wants to stretch their legs\, enjoy some fresh 
 air\, and meet new people.\n\nAfter our walk\, we'll head over to **The Bu
 ll: A Firkin Pub** for brunch and a chance to relax\, chat\, and get to kn
 ow one another. After all\, the walk is just the beginning—the conversat
 ions afterward are where friendships often start.\n\n📲 Don't forget to 
 join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE!](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59m
 SCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll sp
 end about **90 minutes** walking the York Beltline Trail at a comfortable 
 social pace.\nAlong the way we'll enjoy one of Toronto's lesser-known walk
 ing trails\, share some conversation\, and unwind after the workday.\n\nWh
 en we finish\, anyone who would like to is welcome to join us for brunch a
 t **The Bull: A Firkin Pub**. You're also welcome to head home after the w
 alk if you prefer.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk
  happens rain or shine unless severe weather makes it unsafe.\nThe trail i
 s mostly flat and suitable for most fitness levels. Please wear comfortabl
 e walking shoes and bring water if it's a warm evening.\n\nThis is a **soc
 ial walk**\, not a guided historical tour. I'll share a little history abo
 ut the Beltline along the way\, but the focus is on enjoying the evening t
 ogether.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Out
 side **Caledonia Station (there is only one exit)**\n🫎 I'll be wearing 
 my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **11:00 AM**\n\nI will only wait **5 m
 inutes.**\nEarly is on time.\nOn time is late.\nPlease be on time\, as we 
 will leave promptly.\n\n🏁 **End Point:** Near Davisville Station.\n\n**
 *\n\n## 🍽️ After the Walk\n\nWe'll head to **The Bull: A Firkin Pub**
  for brunch and conversation.\n\n**Menu:** [Click Here!](https://www.firki
 npubs.com/thebullandfirkin/menus/)\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5
  cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto
 :mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis fee helps support the group and allo
 ws us to continue organizing events like this. Thank you for supporting co
 mmunity! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comforta
 ble walking shoes\n🍽️ Money if you'd like to join us for dinner after
 ward.\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone w
 ho wants to be social and make friends—whether single or not.\n\nWe also
  host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽
 ️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\n*
 *REMEMBER:** You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsure ab
 out your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be canc
 elled—please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathe
 w\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **[torontomoviesandou
 tings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come
  for the trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n\n**Leave wondering how
  one of Toronto's oldest railway lines became one of its best hidden walks
 .** 🌿🚶‍♂️🍻
