DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n\\*\\*\\*Please kindly read carefu
 lly\\*\\*\\*\n\nHello everyone\,\n\nCome join us for a beautiful and relax
 ing afternoon by the lake as Soul City Social Club heads to **Oakville for
  a Waterfront Walk\, Talk and Social!**\n\nWe’ll meet near the Oakville 
 waterfront and begin with a few fun and easy ice-breaker games to help eve
 ryone get introduced and comfortable. From there\, we’ll head out for a 
 leisurely walk along the waterfront\, enjoying the harbour\, Lake Ontario\
 , parks and some of the beautiful scenery Oakville has to offer.\n\nThis i
 s a social walk\, not a race! We’ll keep a comfortable pace\, stop along
  the way\, mix up the group and give everyone plenty of opportunities to m
 eet and talk with different people.\n\nThe area also has plenty of cafés\
 , restaurants and boutiques to explore\, along with beautiful tree-lined s
 treets and impressive heritage homes that add to the charm of the walk.\n\
 nJoined by my other groups too\; so we can antiicapte a wonderful day!\n\n
 \\*Many of us will most likely hit a near by pub as well for dinner and be
 verages after\n\n**Location and When to Meet:**\n\\*We will meet outfront 
 Tim Hortons (49 Lakeshore Rd. W) at 4:00 pm-and wait for everyone until 4:
 30 pm (please arrive on time)\n\nMore Details below:\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSte
 ve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\nDetails here:\n\n**Oakville Waterfront Wa
 lk\, Talk and Social!**\n\n• A few fun ice-breaker games near the beginn
 ing to get everyone talking and laughing\n• A leisurely waterfront walk 
 with plenty of time to socialize\n• Beautiful views of Lake Ontario and 
 the Oakville waterfront\n• A chance to meet new people and reconnect wit
 h familiar faces\n• Stops along the way to relax\, chat and enjoy the su
 rroundings\n• A friendly atmosphere welcoming friends\, singles and coup
 les\n• The possibility of grabbing a beverage and/or bite to eat togethe
 r afterward for anyone who wants to continue socializing\n\nWhether you’
 re coming on your own or bringing a friend\, the idea is simple: get outsi
 de\, enjoy the waterfront\, have some good conversations and spend a few h
 ours with some friendly people.\n\nNew members are always welcome\, and if
  you’re attending by yourself\, don’t worry—that’s exactly why we
 ’ll start with some ice-breakers and introductions.\nCome walk\, talk\, 
 laugh and enjoy a little time by the lake!\n\n**Event Fee:**\n\n10 dollars
  (cash only) when you arrive (HST is included)\nor e transfer in advance t
 o [Steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:Steveflemming11@gmail.com)\n\nLots of
  free park on Lakershore and surronding residential area\n\n**Where to Fin
 d Us:**\n\\*We will meet right outfront the **Tim Hortons-** **49 Lakeshor
 e Rd. W-** Feel free to purchase a beverage when you arrive\n\\*Bathrooms 
 provided there too\n\n**Coming from Toronto-Go Train:**\nOakville is easy 
 to reach from Toronto by GO Train. Take the Lakeshore West line from Union
  Station directly to Oakville GO Station\, with the trip taking approximat
 ely 45–50 minutes.
